Wilson N, et al. Acute kidney injury in the era of the AKI E-Alert. Clin J Am Soc Nephrol. 2016;12:2123–2131. doi: 10.2215/CJN.05170516. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. Park S, Baek SH, Ahn S, Lee KH, Hwang H, Ryu J, et al. Impact of electronic acute kidney injury (AKI) alerts with automated nephrologist consultation on detection and severity of AKI: a quality improvement study. Am J Kidney Dis. 2018;1:9–19. doi: 10.1053/j.ajkd.2017.06.008. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 16. Gubb S, Holmes J, Smith G, Geen J, Williams J, Donovan K, Phillips AO. Acute kidney injury in children based on electronic alerts. J Pediatr. 2020;220:14–20.e4. doi: 10.1016/j.jpeds.2019.11.019. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Menon S, Tarrago R, Carlin K, Wu H, Yonekawa K. Impact of integrated clinical decision support systems in the management of pediatric acute kidney injury: a pilot study. Pediatr Res. 2021;5:1164–1170. doi: 10.1038/s41390-020-1046-8. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Supplementary Materials Graphical abstract (PPTX 510 KB) (509.8KB, pptx) Data Availability Statement The datasets generated during and/or analyzed during the current study are available from the corresponding author on reasonable request.',322,'2025-10-15 06:03:39','2025-10-15 06:03:39');
