PubMed ] 28. Lee, J. H., Hong, H., Nam, G., Hwang, E. J. & Park, C. M. Effect of human-AI interaction on detection of malignant lung nodules on chest radiographs. Radiology 307 , e222976 (2023). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 29. Yanagawa, M. et al. Diagnostic performance for pulmonary adenocarcinoma on CT: Comparison of radiologists with and without three-dimensional convolutional neural network. Eur Radiol 31 , 1978–1986 (2021). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 30. Krakowski, I. et al. Human-AI interaction in skin cancer diagnosis: A systematic review and meta-analysis. npj Digit. Med. 7 , 1–10 (2024). [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] 31. Goh, E. et al. ChatGPT Influence on medical decision-making, bias, and equity: A randomized study of clinicians evaluating clinical vignettes. medRxiv e-prints (2023) 10.1101/2023.11.24.23298844. 32. Tschandl, P. et al. Human–computer collaboration for skin cancer recognition. Nat Med 26 , 1229–1234 (2020). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 33. Han, S. S. et al. Evaluation of artificial intelligence-assisted diagnosis of skin neoplasms: A single-center, paralleled, unmasked, randomized controlled trial. J Invest Dermatol 142 , 2353-2362.e2 (2022). [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 34. Cabral, S. et al. Clinical reasoning of a generative artificial intelligence model compared with physicians. JAMA Intern Med 184 , 581 (2024). [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 35. OpenAI et al. GPT-4 technical report. arXiv e-prints (2024) 10.48550/arXiv.2303.08774. 36. Singhal, K. et al. Toward expert-level medical question answering with large language models. Nat Med 31 , 943–950 (2025). [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Associated Data This section collects any data citations, data availability statements, or supplementary materials included in this article. Data Availability Statement The datasets analyzed during this study available from the corresponding author on r